#NEXUS

[ zheng2026a_fig7: Rectangular time tree with a stage scale along the top, silhouettes beside several tips and a palaeogeographic map in the lower right. Proceratosauridae (five tips) and Stokesosauridae (four tips) are each drawn as one vertical with all their branches leaving it: polytomies. The bottom branch of Pantyrannosauria ends in a long empty oval with no name (presumably later tyrannosauroids); it is left out, so its node is not encoded. Clade names printed along the stems are kept; the numbered and coloured ovals (age dates, map localities) are not. 11 tips, 2 polytomies (5, 4 children); 4 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Sample 10 case (census 3, seed 20261274). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

